---
import Site from '../layouts/Site.astro';
import ClaimBlock from '../components/ClaimBlock.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import { release, url } from '../lib/publication';
const forecast = release.claims.find(c => c.id === 'C-IMD-OUTLOOK-20260831');
const rain = release.claims.find(c => c.id === 'C-IMD-RAINFALL-DEP-india-20260923');
const storage = release.claims.find(c => c.id === 'C-CWC-INDIA-STORAGE-20260910');
---
<Site title="What happens next?" description="A dated official forecast, conditional pathways and the observations needed to judge recovery.">
  <PageHeader title="The next signal matters" eyebrow="Outlook and recovery" description="An outlook proposes what may happen. An observation records what has happened. A scenario explains how several conditions could interact." />
  <section class="section"><div class="shell page-grid"><article>
    <h2>First, separate the clocks.</h2><div class="grid-2"><div class="editorial-card story-step"><p class="eyebrow">Forecast · issued 31 August 2026</p><h3>A dated September outlook</h3><p>IMD forecast all-India September rainfall as most likely below normal, its category for under 91% of the 1971–2020 September average. It also identified places where normal or above-normal rain was possible. The issue covers September 2026, subject to any later IMD issue. We have not checked whether one exists. <a href={forecast ? url(`/sources/${forecast.evidenceIds[0]}/`) : url('/sources/')}>Original outlook ↗</a></p></div><div class="editorial-card story-step"><p class="eyebrow">Observed · through 23 September 2026</p><h3>A partial season measurement</h3><p>IMD's all-India graphic reported 713.3 mm since 1 June against 837.7 mm normal for those dates, a rounded −14.9% departure. It is not a measured outcome for the whole of September. <a href={rain ? url(`/sources/${rain.evidenceIds[0]}/`) : url('/sources/')}>Observation record ↗</a></p></div></div>
    <h2>How could a local problem deepen?</h2><p><strong>Illustrative scenario, not a prediction:</strong> if low rain persists in a supply catchment, usable storage or groundwater fails to replenish, withdrawals remain high, and delivery is interrupted, a particular service area could face greater strain. Each link needs a dated local record. This scenario has no assigned probability and does not describe all India.</p>
    <h2>How could concern ease?</h2><p>Sustained catchment replenishment, rising usable storage within a stable monitored cohort, recovering groundwater observations and restored service would all matter. A rainy day by itself is not evidence that a tap is reliable or safe. A full reservoir elsewhere may not serve the affected community.</p>
    <div class="figure"><p class="eyebrow">Signals to watch together</p><div class="table-wrap"><table class="data-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Question</th><th scope="col">Record needed</th><th scope="col">Current status here</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Did the catchment refill?</td><td>Matched daily rain and runoff, same boundary and dates.</td><td>Only broad IMD rainfall approved.</td></tr><tr><td>Is usable water available?</td><td>Reservoir cohort, live capacity and dated groundwater wells.</td><td>One dated 10 September monitored-reservoir snapshot; no approved current trend or groundwater series. {storage && <a href={url(`/sources/${storage.evidenceIds[0]}/`)}>CWC bulletin ↗</a>}</td></tr><tr><td>Did people receive safe service?</td><td>Utility hours, volume and quality tests in the same service area.</td><td>No September 2026 measure.</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>
    <div class="note"><strong>Current forecast status</strong><p>The 31 August issue's stated horizon runs through September 2026. We have not verified whether a later IMD issue updates it. <a href="https://mausam.imd.gov.in/">Check IMD for current bulletins ↗</a>.</p></div>
  </article><aside><p class="eyebrow">Read next</p><a href={url('/explore/')}>Rainfall observations</a><a href={url('/response/')}>Documented response</a><a href={url('/data-status/')}>Freshness and missing series</a></aside></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="shell reading"><p class="eyebrow">Source-linked forecast record</p>{forecast && <ClaimBlock claim={forecast} heading="31 August issue; valid for September 2026" />}</div></section>
</Site>
